WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.160
Your Mac gets exactly one default browser.

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.140
Your links don't all belong in it.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.480
Junction takes that default spot,

4
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:13.450
and sends every link you click to the right browser, the right profile, or the right app.

5
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.010
You write the rules once.

6
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.660
Match a domain, a wildcard, even the app you clicked in.

7
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.080
First match wins.

8
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.190
Not sure where a link will land?

9
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.130
Paste it in.

10
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.920
Junction strips the tracking junk, then shows the exact rule that catches it.

11
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.660
Clicked in Slack instead?

12
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.240
A different rule takes it.

13
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:32.600
Want to choose?

14
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.420
Hold Option as you click, and Junction asks, right at your cursor.

15
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:42.390
Zoom, Slack, Figma and Spotify links can skip the browser, and open straight in their apps.

16
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.470
Flip rules on and off from the menu bar,

17
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.940
keep them in a JSON file you own,

18
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.720
and sync them across your Macs with iCloud.

19
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:51.760
Junction.

20
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.130
Free, open source, zero telemetry.

21
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.040
Every link, in the right place.
